      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is LINQ?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "LINQ (Language Integrated Query) provides a consistent query syntax for collections, databases, and XML directly in C#."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "LINQ provides query capabilities using SQL-like syntax or method syntax. Supports filtering, sorting, grouping, and aggregation. Works with any IEnumerable<T> or IQueryable<T>."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "LINQ Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "// Method syntax\nvar adults = people\n    .Where(p => p.Age >= 18)\n    .OrderBy(p => p.Name)\n    .Select(p => new { p.Name, p.Age });\n\n// Query syntax\nvar query = from p in people\n            where p.Age >= 18\n            orderby p.Name\n            select p;"
      }
    },
    {
